  "behavior": "A disabled `<fieldset>`, native or `Fieldset.Root`, disables each form part in it as its `disabled` prop does, also with no `Field.Root`. A part in the first `<legend>` child of a native fieldset stays enabled after the mount, as in HTML. `Fieldset.Legend` renders a `<div>`, so a part in it is disabled. A disabled part has `data-disabled`, the native `disabled` or `aria-disabled`, and the `disabled` slot state. A press, Space or a stepper button changes no value, Tab and the arrow keys skip the part, and `Form` leaves out its value. The parts follow each later change of a native fieldset. Each part that renders a native button follows the fieldset too, and a disabled trigger cannot open its popup on hover. A `ToggleGroup` in a disabled fieldset has `data-disabled` and the `disabled` slot state, as its native toggles do. Base UI follows only `Fieldset.Root`, through `Field.Root`. In a native disabled fieldset, its controls show no disabled state, Tab focuses a radio, a checkbox or a switch, and a press or Space changes its value. Its native buttons get no fieldset state, and its hover triggers can open their popups.",
  "dueWith": "packages/react/src/radio-group/RadioGroup.tsx"
}
